---
description: File Naming Conventions
globs: "**/*.ts"
alwaysApply: true
---
- Use the module name as prefix and type as suffix (e.g., user.service.ts)
- Example files for User module: user.module.ts, {{#if isGraphQL}}user.resolver.ts{{/if}}{{#if isRest}}user.controller.ts{{/if}}, user.service.ts{{#if isMongoose}}, user.repository.ts, user.schema.ts{{/if}}
{{#if isGraphQL}}- For GraphQL, use *.object.ts for output types and *.input.ts for input types{{/if}}
{{#if isRest}}- For REST, use *.dto.ts for data transfer objects{{/if}}
- If multiple files share the same type, organize them in a dedicated folder (e.g., inputs/, dto/)
